  "trackedSecrets": "A parity row has no placeholders. Its tracked secrets on a path are the tokens of its input (runs of letters, digits and . _ ~ + / % -, with those seven punctuation characters trimmed from both ends, 4 or more characters long) that main's output on that path no longer contains, except key words, plus any declaredSecrets for the row. A token is a key word when every part of it, split at - _ . and at a lower-to-upper case change, is in keyWords, case ignored. So a key or scheme word that main swallows is never a secret, and a value that main keeps, such as a build number, is never tracked. declaredSecrets can only add secrets; nothing removes one.",
